## Why This Is Asked
Assesses understanding of idempotency, asynchronous processing, and polling reliability in a real API flow. It also probes concurrency handling, error scenarios, and test tooling choices.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys and deduplication
- Asynchronous processing with 202 and Location for polling
- Polling strategy with timeout and backoff
- Concurrency and race condition handling
- Auth, validation, and rate-limiting tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Jest + supertest snippet for idempotent create
const res1 = await request(app).post('/payments')
  .set('Idempotency-Key', 'abc-123')
  .set('Authorization', 'Bearer token')
  .send({ amount: 1000, currency: 'USD' });
expect(res1.status).toBe(202);
const id = res1.body.paymentId;
const res2 = await request(app).post('/payments')
  .set('Idempotency-Key', 'abc-123')
  .set('Authorization', 'Bearer token')
  .send({ amount: 1000, currency: 'USD' });
expect(res2.status).toBe(202);
```

